          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KUMQ7eUjc5LEcE8qRtZN1w",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: The architectural pattern of centralizing all startup decisions\u2014credentials, paths, and configuration\u2014in one place to enable security, consistency, and controlled downstream propagation.\\ntimestamp: 2025-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - pattern/Single-Point-of-Control\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages explicitly describe single-point-of-control patterns for their respective domains (credentials and file paths); the connection between them as instances of the same architectural principle is direct and explicit in both pages\u0027 language.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2026-01-14\\n---\\n\\nGrimoire\u0027s architecture centralizes critical decisions\u2014where secrets live and where files live\u2014at a single startup composition point rather than scattering them across the codebase.\\n\\n## Credential Scoping\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] applies this pattern to secrets: the Anthropic API key is never held in the Hub\u0027s own process environment. Instead, a local secrets loader reads the key and injects it only into the child process environment of the Ingest and Query agents immediately before they start. The Hub\u0027s process is never mutated; a compromised Hub cannot leak the credential simply by reading its own environment.\\n\\n## Runtime Paths\\n\\n[[runtime-paths]] applies the same pattern to file locations: every file-system path the Hub touches at runtime\u2014the wiki root, data directories, databases, the secrets file, and agent instruction directories\u2014is resolved in exactly one place at startup. A single path resolver reads configuration (command line, environment, config file, or code defaults), validates everything exists, auto-creates writable directories, and reports the effective value and source. Downstream code never rediscovers paths on its own; it consumes already-resolved values instead.\\n\\n## The Pattern\\n\\nBoth decisions follow the same principle: **move critical configuration decisions to a single startup point, validate them there, and then pass resolved values downstream**. This achieves three things:\\n\\n1. **Security/correctness by architecture**: Secrets can\u0027t leak from the Hub if the Hub never holds them; paths can\u0027t drift if every component uses the resolver\u0027s output.\\n2. **Auditability**: The composition point logs its decisions (source, effective value); downstream behavior becomes predictable.\\n3. **Extensibility without sprawl**: Adding a new credential scope or a new runtime location means extending the resolver once, not scattering logic across the codebase.\\n\\nThe pattern applies equally to secrets and file paths because both are critical, should be centrally validated, and should be propagated\u2014not rediscovered\u2014downstream.\\n\u0022}"
        },
