      "assistant_text": "The index update is being blocked by a policy check. However, the core synthesis page has been created successfully. Let me answer your question with the connection I found:\n\n---\n\n## The Connection\n\nYour credential-scoping and runtime-path decisions are **instances of the same architectural pattern**: centralizing all critical decisions at a single startup composition point.\n\n**[[credential-scoping]]** applies this pattern to secrets: the Anthropic API key is never held in the Hub\u0027s own process. Instead, a secrets loader injects it only into the child process environments of Ingest and Query agents immediately before they start. The Hub\u0027s process is never mutated\u2014so a compromised Hub cannot leak the credential by reading its own environment.\n\n**[[runtime-paths]]** applies the exact same pattern to file locations: every runtime path the Hub touches\u2014the wiki root, data directories, the database, the secrets file, and agent instruction directories\u2014is resolved in one place at startup. A single path resolver reads configuration, validates it all exists, auto-creates writable directories, and reports effective values. Downstream code never rediscovers paths; it uses already-resolved values.\n\n**Why this matters together:**\n\nBoth decisions follow the principle: **move critical configuration decisions to a single startup point, validate them there, and propagate resolved values downstream rather than letting each component rediscover them.**\n\nThis achieves three things:\n1. **Security/correctness by architecture** \u2014 secrets can\u0027t leak from the Hub if the Hub never holds them; paths can\u0027t drift if everything uses the resolver\u0027s output.\n2. **Auditability** \u2014 the composition point logs its decisions; downstream behavior is predictable.\n3. **Extensibility** \u2014 adding a new credential or path means extending the resolver once, not scattering logic across the codebase.\n\nI\u0027ve saved this connection as a new page, **[[concepts/single-composition-point]]**. The index update encountered a technical issue, but the synthesis page itself was created successfully and captures this pattern for future reference.",
